C_{d} = \frac{1}{\frac{1}{2}\rho^{f}U_\mathrm{0}^\mathrm{2}D}\int_{\Gamma^{fs}} (\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{f}\cdot \boldsymbol{n})\cdot \boldsymbol{n}_{x} \mathrm{d\Gamma}, \quad
\end{align}
where $C_{l}$ and $C_{d}$ denote the lift and drag coefficients, respectively, and $\boldsymbol{n}_{x}$ and $\boldsymbol{n}_{y}$ are the Cartesian components of the unit outward normal vector $\boldsymbol{n}$.
