\centerline{\includegraphics[scale=0.42]{Fig.pdf}}
\vspace{0mm}
\caption{Visualization of the magnetic field by the color plots (encoding the magnitude of the field) and the force lines (the arrows indicating the directions of the field) for ${B=0.2}$. The top left panel (${m=0}$, ${a=0}$) shows the uniform magnetic field of the Bertotti-Robinson (BR) background universe. Left column corresponds to the Schwarzschild-BR black holes without rotation (${a=0}$), while the right column depicts the general situation for Kerr-BR black holes (${a\not=0}$) with the rotation parameters~${a=0.35, 0.39, 0.399998 }$ (labeled as ${a=0.4}$) and~${m=0.4}$. The horizons are indicated by the black circles, the ergoregions are bounded by the dashed curves. In all the cases the external magnetic field is weakened in the equatorial plane ${\theta=\frac{\pi}{2}}$, and the force lines are ``expelled away'' --- exhibiting the Meissner effect. The blue discs and annuli indicate non-stationary region ${Q<0}$ inside the black hole where the ZAMO observer \eqref{ZAMO} is not timelike and thus the field \eqref{EandB} is not well defined.
}
