	 	By the definition of $\Omega$ and $\alpha_S$, where $S \in \mathcal{A}$, $(\Omega, \geqslant)$ is a directed set. By the assumption, for each $(F, m) \in \Omega$, $\exists$ a $C_{(F, m)} \in \displaystyle{\bigcap_{S \in F}}H_d^-(S, \alpha_S+ 2/m) \setminus H_d^-(S_0,g)$. Consequently, $(C_{(F, m)})_{(F, m) \in \Omega}$ is a net in $CL(X)$. We show that $(C_{(F, m)})$ is $\mathcal{LE}_{\mathcal{S},d}^-$-convergent to $A$ while $\tau_{\mathcal{S},d}^-$-convergence fails. To see $\mathcal{LE}_{\mathcal{S},d}^-$-convergence, let $S_1 \in \mathcal{S}$ and $\epsilon_1 > 0$ be such that $e_d(S_1,A) < \epsilon_1$. 
