	 	So $e_d(S_1, C_{(F,m)}) \leq \alpha_{S_1} + \frac{2}{m_1} < \epsilon_1$ for all $(F,m) \geqslant (\{S_1\}, m)$. 

	 	For $\tau_{\mathcal{S},d}^-$-convergence, observe that $A \in H_d^-(S_0,f)$  while $C_{(F,m)} \notin H_d^-(S_0,g)$ for any $(F,m) \in \Omega$. Therefore, by Theorem \ref{Hittypetheoremforlowertsd}, the $\tau_{\mathcal{S},d}^-$-convergence of $(C_{(F,m)})$ to $A$ fails. 		
