\begin{abstract}

Let $\F$ be a codimension 1 singular holomorphic foliation on $\P^3$ and let $Z$ be the union of the 1-dimensional connected components of its singular set;   Dominique Cerveau asked in 2013 whether  $Z$ is necessarily connected. We prove that if a $k$-dimensional holomorphic foliation on a projective manifold whose determinant bundle of the normal sheaf is ample has a singular set $Z$ of dimension $k-1$, then $Z$ is connected.
%a generalization of it for $k$-dimensional holomorphic foliations, $k > 2$, on projective manifolds with singular set of dimension $k-1$, provided that the determinant bundle of the normal sheaf is ample.
This can be regarded as providing an obstruction for the integrability of singular holomorphic distributions in the spirit of Bott's work.

\end{abstract}



