\end{figure}

In equation (12d) we define $\displaystyle{\Pi_c(L,A_p)= \epsilon_c L+\Phi_c A_p}$. If we assume that the net lipid flux (due to modLDL consumption and efferocytosis) into SMCs is constant, then $\displaystyle{\Pi_c(L,A_p) = \Pi_c}$ is constant and positive. Then from system \eqref{MS} we have a subsystem for SMCs and the SMC total lipid load
\begin{subequations}
	\begin{align}
		&\frac{dC}{dt} = \rho_c\left(1-\frac{C}{C_0}\right)C - \beta_c C -  \delta_c\frac{ A_c^nC}{\alpha_c^nC^n+A_c^n} \\
		&\frac{dA_c}{dt} = \Pi_cC + \rho_c\left(1-\frac{C}{C_0}\right)C - \beta_c A_c - \delta_c \frac{A_c^nA_c}{\alpha_c^nC^n+A_c^n}.
	\end{align}\label{2D}
\end{subequations}
The steady states of the model system \eqref{2D} are given by  \begin{align}
\rho_c\left(1-\frac{C^*}{C_0}\right)C^* - \beta_c C^* -  \delta_c\frac{ {A_c^*}^nC^*}{\alpha_c^n{C^*}^n+{A_c^*}^n} = 0,\label{2D1}
\end{align}
and 
\begin{align}
	\Pi_c C^* + \rho_c\left(1-\frac{C^*}{C_0}\right)C^* - \beta_c{A_c}^* - \delta \frac{{A_c^*}^{n+1}}{\alpha^n{C^*}^n+{A_c^*}^n} = 0.\label{2D2}
\end{align}
This gives $\displaystyle{C^*=0}$ and $\displaystyle{A_c^*=0}$ as one steady-state solution. If $\displaystyle{C^*\neq 0}$ there is a positive steady state $\displaystyle{\left(C^*, A_c^*\right)}$, such that for $\displaystyle{n=1}$
\begin{equation*}
	C^* = C_0\frac{\alpha_c\left(\rho_c-\beta_c\right)+k\left(\rho_c-\beta_c-\delta_c\right)}{\rho_c\left(k+\alpha_c\right)}, \quad\text{and}\quad A_c^* = kC_0\frac{\alpha_c\left(\rho_c-\beta_c\right)+k\left(\rho_c-\beta_c-\delta_c\right)}{\rho_c\left(k+\alpha_c\right)},
\end{equation*}
provided that \begin{equation}
	\rho_c>\beta_c+\frac{\delta_c k}{\alpha_c+k},
\end{equation}
where \begin{equation}
	k = \frac{\Pi_c+\delta_c+\beta_c\left(1-\alpha_c\right)+\sqrt{\left(\Pi_c+\delta_c+\beta_c\left(1-\alpha_c\right)\right)^2+4\left(\beta_c+\delta_c\right)\left(\Pi_c+\beta_c\right)\alpha_c}}{2\left(\beta_c+\delta_c\right)},
\end{equation}
on condition that $\displaystyle{k>1}$ if $\displaystyle{\beta_c<\frac{\Pi_c}{\alpha_c}}$. 

Figure \ref{PPC} presents the phase plane for the system \eqref{2D} for the parameter set in Table 2 and $\displaystyle{\Pi_c}=2.5$. Steady state points are at $\displaystyle{\left(0, 0\right)}$ and $\displaystyle{\left(C^*, A_c^*\right)}$.  When $\displaystyle{\rho_c\le\beta_c+\frac{\delta_c k}{\alpha_c+k}}$, a positive steady state solution does not exist.  When $\displaystyle{\rho_c>\beta_c+\frac{\delta_c k}{\alpha_c+k}}$, the steady state $\displaystyle{\left(0,0\right)}$ appears to be a saddle point and the positive steady state exists. This implies that in an environment where smooth muscle cell proliferation is not enough to dominate the combined effects of apoptosis and phenotype switching, SMCs will migrate into the intima leaving none to form the cap. 

