    Left: A contour map of the variance reduction ratio $r(\rho,c)$ as a function of the correlation $\rho = \sigma_g / \sigma_f$ and relative cost $c = c_g / c_f$. 
    The red curve indicates the level set $r(\rho,c) = 1$; the regimes where PEMC outperforms standard MC lie below the curve. 
