Since the volume and area law contributions for the entropy cancel out in the Markov tripartition, the Markov CMI is dictated by $\Delta S(q)$:
\begin{align}
    &I(A:C|B) \nonumber \\ & =  \Delta S_{BC}(q) + \Delta S_{AB}(q) - \Delta S_B(q) - \Delta S_{ABC}(q) \\
    & \approx \log(2)e^{-|\overline{B}|/\xi(q)} (1 - e^{-|\overline{A}|/\xi(q)})(1 - e^{-|\overline{C}|/\xi(q)})
